Processing, structure, properties and useful performance (@mat-process-chain: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @materials-engineering, #source "../sources/Materiais-de-Construcao-Mecanica-Zolin.lingua#r_1KS5EGZJ8PBFDART80K21J1309", #source "../sources/Fundamentals-of-Materials-Science-MIT-3-012.lingua#r_1JE4A3P3KKM0FZXERWFATXCS1Z", #source "../sources/Materials-Structure-and-Observation-DoITPoMS.lingua#r_57315283EDNWKYC1PQE23G2AKF", #materials-engineering "Separate-material-response-from-component-geometry.lingua#r_0E6J5YFEH99D8D3HF96JG49W64") { r_35NBQ2E68RTBTH1HRMWD0H1KDB
**Read:** [Materiais de Construção Mecânica — Zolin](../sources/Materiais-de-Construcao-Mecanica-Zolin.lingua#r_1KS5EGZJ8PBFDART80K21J1309), thermal treatments and fabrication; [Fundamentals of Materials Science — MIT 3.012](../sources/Fundamentals-of-Materials-Science-MIT-3-012.lingua#r_1JE4A3P3KKM0FZXERWFATXCS1Z), orientation and the structure/bonding overview; [Materials structure and observation — Cambridge DoITPoMS](../sources/Materials-Structure-and-Observation-DoITPoMS.lingua#r_57315283EDNWKYC1PQE23G2AKF), atomic-scale structure.

Follow a proposed causal chain: composition and processing establish structure; structure and service conditions affect properties; properties interact with geometry and interfaces to produce performance. Feedback also runs in the other direction: a required function motivates a structure or process change.

An alloy heat treatment can change precipitates, residual stress and dimensions. Drawing a polymer can orient chains. A ceramic firing schedule can change porosity and phases. Those changes do not all improve every property at once. The useful comparison is tied to a function and its operating conditions.

**Work:** Draw this chain for a metal spring, a polymer package and a ceramic insulator. Identify a measurable quantity at each link and an alternative explanation for an observed performance difference. Trace the energy, equipment and knowledge needed to repeat the processing, including what must be transferred to the next producer or user.

**Return:** [Materials engineering](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
